Package: smart-disk-analyzer
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Abbas Paliwala <abbaspaliwala@users.noreply.github.com>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: nodejs (>= 18.13), smartmontools, pkexec | policykit-1, xdg-utils
Recommends: zenity | kdialog | x11-utils, udisks2
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/abbaspaliwala/SMART-Disk-Analyzer
Description: SMART disk health dashboard with remaining-life forecasting
 Reads every SMART parameter of every disk, scores the health of each drive and
 forecasts its remaining useful life in a local web dashboard.
 .
 Features:
  * all ATA attributes, NVMe health-log fields and SCSI counters, filterable
  * health score with the risk factors that produced it
  * remaining-life forecast from wear trend, write budget and defect growth
  * partition map with one-click access to mounted volumes
  * snapshot history and canvas trend charts
 .
 Reading SMART needs raw device access, so the server is started through
 PolicyKit after one authentication prompt, binds to 127.0.0.1 only and stores
 its snapshot history in /var/lib/smart-disk-analyzer/.
